'''''Populus simonii''''', '''Simon's poplar''', '''Simon poplar''', or '''Chinese cottonwood''', is a species of [[Populus|poplar]] native to northeast China and to Mongolia, and commonly planted as a [[street tree]] in cool temperate areas of Europe.<ref>{{cite book |date= 2005-05-20|title= Urban Forests and Trees: A Reference Book|isbn=9783540251262  |last1= Cecil C|last2= Nilsson|first2= Kjell|last3= Randrup|first3= Thomas B|last4= Schipperijn|first4= Jasper|publisher= Springer}}</ref> There have been introductions into North America, South Africa, Australia and New Zealand.

